# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# Local environment overrides
#
# The two build-target files are committed on purpose: `.env.native` and
# `.env.desktop` each hold a single non-secret flag (`VITE_BUILD_TARGET`) that
# says which shape of the game is being bundled, the tests read them, and they
# are part of how the mobile and desktop builds are made. A plain `.env` is the
# file a developer keeps local overrides in, and nothing in the game reads one,
# so it belongs to a machine rather than to the project. `.env.local` is already
# covered by `*.local` above.
.env

# Desktop (Electron) build output
#
# Three directories, all generated, none of them part of the game: the compiled
# shell and its preload (`desktop/build`, CommonJS output of `tsconfig.desktop.json`),
# the desktop renderer bundle (`desktop/renderer`, the same game the website
# ships, built with `--mode desktop`), and the installer electron-builder writes
# (`desktop-release`). Kept apart from `dist/` on purpose: that is the website
# Cloudflare Pages deploys, and a desktop build must never be able to overwrite
# it.
desktop/build/
desktop/renderer/
desktop-release/

# Archives and exports
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Test and tool caches
coverage/
.vitest/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tooling scratch (agent/IDE working files, not part of the game)
.freebuff/

# Browser-harness output (screenshots and JSON read off a local run, regenerated
# by the scripts in .freebuff/ui-test/)
band/
contrast/
gradients/
rail/
screens/

# Soak reports (developer output, regenerated by `npm run soak`)
soak-reports/

# Release signing material
#
# A keystore in git is a keystore everybody has, so the Android upload key, the
# properties file that points at it, the Apple certificates, and any Play
# service account JSON stay out of the repository. `keystore.properties.example`
# is the committed shape of the ignored file, and `npm run android:preflight`
# fails if a secret has ever been tracked rather than merely written down.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
keystore.properties
play-service-account.json

# The Discord bot token
#
# The token that configures the game's community server is a credential like any
# other: it acts as the bot, which can post as itself and read every channel it
# can see. A token in git is a token in every clone and in every fork for ever,
# and unlike a leaked keystore there is nothing to re-upload afterwards — the
# only fix is to reset the token and invite the bot again. `discord.env.example`
# is the committed shape of the ignored file, and `npm run discord:plan` refuses
# to run at all if `discord.env` has ever been tracked rather than merely written
# down.
discord.env

# Signed store artifacts. They are built, uploaded and deleted, never kept:
# Play distributes the bundle and the App Store distributes the archive.
*.aab
*.apk
*.ipa
